sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Proposed offline write and encrypted delivery
  accDescr: Local save, relay acknowledgement and application on another device are separate. Durable operation identity precedes sealing. Retries reuse stored ciphertext. Incoming records and cursors commit together.
  participant UI as 📱 Device A UI
  participant DB as Local repository
  participant Core as Replica + Rust crypto
  participant Relay as Opaque relay
  participant B as Trusted device B
  UI->>DB: Transaction: operation ID, projection, pending seal
  DB-->>UI: Locally saved, not yet synced
  Note over DB,Core: Offline work survives restart. Encryption at rest is a separate requirement
  DB->>Core: Durable operation + trusted membership checkpoint
  Core-->>DB: Candidate authenticated ciphertext + checkpoint precondition
  DB->>DB: Transaction: compare checkpoint and store ciphertext/outbox
  Note over DB,Core: Changed checkpoint means discard candidate and reseal. Never upload it
  loop Until authenticated relay receipt
    DB->>Relay: Upload identical stored bytes and operation ID
    Relay-->>DB: Durable relay receipt or retryable failure
  end
  DB->>DB: Persist relay delivery status
  Note over Relay,B: Relay ACK does not mean another device applied the operation
  B->>Relay: Fetch bounded batch after delivery cursor
  Relay-->>B: Envelopes and candidate cursor
  B->>B: Authenticate, validate membership, resolve or quarantine
  B->>B: Transaction: records, projection/conflict, checkpoint, cursor
  Note over DB,B: Same valid operations converge or produce the same explicit conflict
